INSERT INTO `interview_answers` VALUES (1,'In my e-commerce microservices platform, I structured the backend into layered architecture with Controllers, Service layers, and JPA Repositories. Data persistence is managed via Spring Data JPA and Hibernate connected to MySQL with HikariCP connection pooling. For transactional integrity, I used declarative @Transactional boundaries and optimistic locking with @Version to handle concurrent inventory deductions.','2026-10-27 15:11:39.578293',1,1,1),(2,'In Java concurrency, synchronized blocks provide mutual exclusion and establish a happens-before relationship, ensuring both atomicity and visibility across threads. Volatile guarantees memory visibility directly with main memory, preventing CPU cache staleness and instruction reordering, but does not guarantee compound atomicity. For lock-free atomic operations, AtomicInteger and AtomicReference utilize hardware CPU Compare-And-Swap (CAS) instructions for high concurrency.','2026-10-27 15:11:39.691858',2,1,1),(3,'To diagnose slow queries in MySQL, I first enable the slow query log and inspect the query execution plan using EXPLAIN. I check for full table scans and examine key usage. I create composite B-tree indexes covering WHERE and ORDER BY columns, avoid SELECT * to minimize I/O overhead, and leverage Redis caching for frequently read immutable reference data to keep response latency below 50ms.','2026-10-27 15:11:39.740476',3,1,1),(4,'(No answer provided)','2026-10-27 16:22:33.646656',4,2,2),(5,'(No answer provided)','2026-10-27 16:22:35.150418',5,2,2),(6,'(No answer provided)','2026-10-27 16:22:37.182672',6,2,2),(7,'(No answer provided)','2026-10-27 16:22:38.116643',7,2,2),(8,'(No answer provided)','2026-10-27 16:22:39.344479',8,2,2),(9,'(No answer provided)','2026-11-01 04:44:34.605774',9,3,3),(10,'(No answer provided)','2026-11-01 04:44:34.632809',10,3,3),(11,'(No answer provided)','2026-11-01 04:44:34.657909',11,3,3),(12,'(No answer provided)','2026-11-01 04:44:34.684404',12,3,3),(13,'(No answer provided)','2026-11-01 04:44:34.718458',13,3,3),(14,'In high-throughput microservices, ConcurrentHashMap provides lock striping and CAS updates on tree bins, allowing high read concurrency without blocking entire table buckets. We benchmarked this to sustain 50,000 req/sec. Additionally, volatile memory barriers prevent CPU instruction reordering.','2026-11-01 05:18:42.603731',14,4,4),(15,'Kafka distributed partitions','2026-11-01 05:18:42.523708',15,4,4),(16,'','2026-11-01 05:18:43.674466',16,4,4),(17,'In high-throughput microservices, ConcurrentHashMap provides lock striping and CAS updates on tree bins, allowing high read concurrency without blocking entire table buckets. We benchmarked this to sustain 50,000 req/sec. Additionally, volatile memory barriers prevent CPU instruction reordering.','2026-11-01 05:22:42.453750',17,5,4),(18,'Kafka distributed partitions','2026-11-01 05:22:42.301115',18,5,4),(19,'','2026-11-01 05:22:44.349162',19,5,4),(20,'aasadbfbdsfgfdsgd','2026-11-01 05:27:32.735674',20,6,3),(21,'hjhgf','2026-11-01 05:27:38.789108',21,6,3),(22,'jkhkjhkj','2026-11-01 05:27:43.405095',22,6,3),(23,'n','2026-11-01 05:27:48.009528',23,6,3),(24,'kkk','2026-11-01 05:27:52.544300',24,6,3),(25,'I employ decentralized decision-making frameworks with clear architectural boundaries, empowering engineering managers while aligning quarterly OKRs. We also measure DORA metrics.','2026-11-01 05:35:35.743389',25,7,6),(26,'Agile Scrum with bi-weekly sprints','2026-11-01 05:35:35.664424',26,7,6),(27,'','2026-11-01 05:35:35.835558',27,7,6),(28,'I employ decentralized decision-making frameworks with clear architectural boundaries, empowering engineering managers while aligning quarterly OKRs. We also measure DORA metrics.','2026-11-01 05:36:30.377333',28,8,7),(29,'Agile Scrum with bi-weekly sprints','2026-11-01 05:36:30.293047',29,8,7),(30,'','2026-11-01 05:36:30.483448',30,8,7),(31,'In high-throughput microservices, ConcurrentHashMap provides lock striping and CAS updates on tree bins, allowing high read concurrency without blocking entire table buckets. We benchmarked this to sustain 50,000 req/sec. Additionally, volatile memory barriers prevent CPU instruction reordering.','2026-11-01 05:58:34.829227',31,9,4),(32,'Kafka distributed partitions','2026-11-01 05:58:34.703708',32,9,4),(33,'','2026-11-01 05:58:35.196439',33,9,4);
